"Output" means maps, meshes, textures and other work you create with the Tool
using assets that you own or have separately licensed.

2. PERMITTED USE
You may download, install, execute and privately modify the Tool to create your
own commercial or noncommercial projects, provided you comply with attribution.
You may make only the local, build, version-control and backup copies reasonably
necessary for that use. Your employees and contractors may access such private
copies solely on your behalf, under these same restrictions. This is not a right
to sublicense, assign or transfer this license or distribute the Tool to others.

3. YOUR OUTPUT AND EMBEDDED RUNTIME SHADERS
You retain your rights in your own Output. You may sell, publish, distribute and
otherwise commercially exploit your own Output, including in games and client
projects. You may include the Tool's runtime shaders in compiled/embedded form
only as necessary to display that Output in an end-user project. That exception
does not permit distribution of editor code, a reusable shader/source package,
the Tool itself, or an editor/map-authoring product derived from it. Your Output
must not contain the restricted example assets unless separately licensed.

4. REQUIRED ATTRIBUTION
Each distributed project made using the Tool must contain a reasonably visible
credit in its credits, About screen, bundled NOTICE or accompanying documentation:
